.TH BYTE_UPPER 3
.SH NAME
byte_upper \- convert a byte array to uppercase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "void byte_upper(void* " s ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_upper
converts all lowercase ASCII characters ('a'-'z') within the memory area
pointed to by
.I s
of length
.I len
to their corresponding uppercase ASCII characters ('A'-'Z').
.PP
The conversion is performed in-place. Other characters remain unchanged. The function does not assume any locale-specific behavior and is restricted to the standard ASCII character set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_lower (3)